							],
							"documentation": "Entry: UC04 has already called ShowApplication(product, configuration). The customer has entered travelerList before ReviewApplication(). No unsupported traveler-input operation is invented.\nScope: successful review and a new, valid, confirmed submission. Existing LoginSession supplies the authenticated memberId; requestKey comes from successful server-side review context.\nReview validates the product, configuration, travelers, capacity and souvenir stock before calculating the displayed finalAmount. historyData is mapped to histories; CalculateApplicationPrice includes regular-customer discount determination. Review performs no save or SMS.\nSubmitTravelApplication runs its data operations inside RunTravelTransaction(productId, work), including repeated validation and amount checks. The callback, lock, duplicate-request and rollback internals are not drawn. All saves and contact selection precede commit; SendDepartureConfirmation occurs only after commit.\nHoneymoon: exactly two travelers; ConfirmHoneymoonDeparture updates the new application before SaveApplication persists it. There is no shared CountTravelers or product departure-status update for Honeymoon.\nOther themes: CountTravelers counts stored actual travelers, not applications. UpdateDepartureStatus confirms at three or more, retains Unconfirmed below three and retains an existing Confirmed status. Shared capacity remains ten.\nFindApplications supplies applicant contacts. Honeymoon or an already-confirmed shared-tour addition selects the new applicant; a newly-confirmed shared tour selects all applicants, deduplicated by memberId; an unconfirmed departure selects no recipients. Recipient selection is not expanded into additional branches.\nSendDepartureConfirmation owns message construction, sending, recording results and retry policy. SMS failure does not undo the committed application or departure state.\nOmitted: detailed field/configuration/capacity/stock validation and correction flows; price/discount failure; persistence failure; transaction, duplicate-request, rollback and re-review internals; separate shared-tour threshold/previous-status and recipient-selection branches; SMS client calls, failure recording and up to three retries; explicit discount-condition branches and traveler field editing.",
